; `emacro` in declaration position, and an invocation matching no
; expression rule (MAC-LANG-14 wide half, MAC-LANG-18).
;
; An `emacro` template is one expression; a declaration position needs
; declarations, so the invocation is `AX3027` at the use. An invocation
; matching no rule is `AX3018` naming every shape the macro accepts.
(emacro esimp ((esimp (+ a 0)) a)
  ((esimp other) other))

(esimp (+ 1 0))

(esimp)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (esimp 1 2 3))
